commit 52bc66294141d6b26e86903d49ce7b41583bc407

C03: the clipboard write final carries the written text and must report the copy, not echo it (CLIPBOARD1361)

CLIPBOARD1359 measured H0199 and H0356: the write was proposed with the exact literal, approved, completed and verified, but the Spanish final after the confirmation was a bare echo («Hola», «Hola mundo», «Buen día.») because the visible payload of clipboard.write.text carried only sequenceNumber, characterCount and changed.

llm._compose_situation_payload: for a verified clipboard.write.text the written literal (grounded by literal_clipboard_write_text from the same request and verified by the provider's post-read) enters the narrator's copy as writtenText.
llm._payload_fact_defect: missing_written_text when the final does not quote that text; echo_without_report when it repeats the text without saying it was copied. Hints for both retries.

No .NET change. Offline probe only; tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


